;;; subject: opendev-terminal-agent-2603 2.2.2 Agent Runtime Architecture: how the assembled agent turns a stateless model into a tool-using agent: the central loop, its surrounding subsystems, and the two modes
;;; made-from: doc_Base012/docs/Papers-AgentHarness/opendev-terminal-agent/02_agent-core/02_agent-core.lisp / s15 .. s22
;;; members: intro cycle io subsystems modes routing plan-subagent planner-stages plan-review normal replan old-design new-design
;;; elsewhere: none
;;; left-out: the captions of Figures 4 and 5
(defrule runtime -> runtime-intro runtime-cycle runtime-io runtime-subsystems runtime-modes runtime-routing runtime-plan-subagent runtime-planner-stages runtime-plan-review runtime-normal runtime-replan runtime-old-design runtime-new-design)
(defrule runtime-intro -> :nucleus runtime-intro/n :elaboration-additional runtime-intro/a1)
(defrule runtime-intro/n -> :instruction "組み立て後のエージェントが動く準備ができたことと、ハーネスの働きを 1 文で書く" :sample "With scaffolding complete, the assembled agent is ready to process user messages.")
(defrule runtime-intro/a1 -> :instruction "中心のループと、その周りの部品の関係を図で示すと書く" :sample "Figure 4 maps this harness architecture: the ReAct execution loop at the center, surrounded by the subsystems that feed it, constrain it, and persist its work.")
(defrule runtime-cycle -> :nucleus runtime-cycle/n :elaboration-additional runtime-cycle/a1 :elaboration-additional runtime-cycle/a2 :elaboration-additional runtime-cycle/a3)
(defrule runtime-cycle/n -> :instruction "中心のループが 1 回の繰り返しで行う段階を挙げて 1 文で書く" :sample "The ReAct loop at the center of Figure 4 executes six phases per iteration: pre-check and compaction, thinking, self-critique, action, tool execution, and post-processing.")
(defrule runtime-cycle/a1 -> :instruction "各段階が実行部の中で担う仕事を 1 文で書く" :sample "Each phase is a distinct stage in the executor pipeline: pre-check drains injected messages and compacts under memory pressure, thinking and self-critique produce optional chain-of-thought traces, the action phase calls the LLM with full tool schemas, tool execution dispatches calls through the registry with approval checks, and post-processing decides whether to iterate or return.")
(defrule runtime-cycle/a2 -> :instruction "繰り返しがいつ終わるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "The cycle repeats until the agent produces a final text response with no tool calls, or until a safety cap is reached.")
(defrule runtime-cycle/a3 -> :instruction "詳しい説明がどの節にあるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Section 2.2.6 details the per-phase algorithms and control flow.")
(defrule runtime-io -> :nucleus runtime-io/n :elaboration-additional runtime-io/a1 :elaboration-additional runtime-io/a2)
(defrule runtime-io/n -> :instruction "上端の入力を受ける部分と、その性質を 1 文で書く" :sample "At the top of Figure 4, the Input Layer accepts user messages through a thread-safe bounded queue, allowing follow-up messages to arrive while the agent is mid-execution.")
(defrule runtime-io/a1 -> :instruction "設定が入力とともに何を渡すかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Configuration and settings flow in alongside the message queue, providing the agent with its runtime parameters (model selection, approval level, working directory).")
(defrule runtime-io/a2 -> :instruction "下端の後処理が担う 3 つの仕事を 1 文で書く" :sample "At the bottom, the Post-Processing path handles three responsibilities after the loop terminates: persisting the updated conversation to the session store, executing any registered Stop hooks, and returning the agent’s final response to the UI layer for rendering.")
(defrule runtime-subsystems -> :nucleus runtime-subsystems/n :elaboration-additional runtime-subsystems/a1 :elaboration-additional runtime-subsystems/a2 :elaboration-additional runtime-subsystems/a3 :elaboration-additional runtime-subsystems/a4 :elaboration-additional runtime-subsystems/a5 :elaboration-additional runtime-subsystems/a6)
(defrule runtime-subsystems/n -> :instruction "周辺の部品の数と、各部品が別の関心を担うことを 1 文で書く" :sample "The periphery of Figure 4 shows seven subsystems, each addressing a distinct concern and detailed in a dedicated section.")
(defrule runtime-subsystems/a1 -> :instruction "指示文を組み立てる部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "The Prompt Composition engine (Section 2.3.1) assembles the system prompt from modular sections (identity, safety policy, tool guidance, workflow rules, and dynamic context), split into cacheable and non-cacheable segments for efficient API caching.")
(defrule runtime-subsystems/a2 -> :instruction "道具の呼び出しを配る部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "The Tool Registry (Section 2.4.1) dispatches each tool call to specialized handlers, with MCP tools discovered lazily at runtime.")
(defrule runtime-subsystems/a3 -> :instruction "安全を担う部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "The Safety System (Section 2.1) provides defense in depth through multiple independent layers, where no single layer is relied upon exclusively and each catches a different failure mode.")
(defrule runtime-subsystems/a4 -> :instruction "文脈を有限の資源として扱う部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "Context Engineering (Section 2.3.6) manages the conversation as a finite resource, applying progressively aggressive compaction as token usage grows.")
(defrule runtime-subsystems/a5 -> :instruction "会話と学んだ戦略を保存する部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "Memory and Session services (Section 2.5) persist both the conversation transcript and a playbook of learned strategies that evolve based on feedback.")
(defrule runtime-subsystems/a6 -> :instruction "専門の仕事を別のエージェントへ任せる部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "Subagent Orchestration (Section 2.2.7) enables the main agent to delegate specialized tasks (code exploration, security review, web generation) to isolated agent instances that share the same tool infrastructure but operate with filtered tool access and independent conversation histories.")
(defrule runtime-modes -> :nucleus runtime-modes/n)
(defrule runtime-modes/n -> :instruction "設計上の要になる決定として、二つのモードで動くことを 1 文で書く" :sample "The key architectural decision is that the system operates in two distinct modes, Plan Mode and Normal Mode, with the agent transitioning between them based on user commands or prompt triggers.")
(defrule runtime-routing -> :nucleus runtime-routing/n :elaboration-additional runtime-routing/a1 :elaboration-additional runtime-routing/a2 :elaboration-additional runtime-routing/a3)
(defrule runtime-routing/n -> :instruction "プロンプトが来たときに、どちらのモードで始めるかを決めることを 1 文で書く" :sample "When a user prompt arrives, the MainAgent checks whether it should enter Plan Mode or proceed directly in Normal Mode.")
(defrule runtime-routing/a1 -> :instruction "計画モードに入る二つの引き金を 1 文で書く" :sample "Two triggers activate Plan Mode: an explicit /plan command from the user, or a heuristic that detects planning intent in the prompt (e.g., requests to “design,” “architect,” or “plan” a change).")
(defrule runtime-routing/a2 -> :instruction "引き金が無いときの扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "All other prompts proceed in Normal Mode by default.")
(defrule runtime-routing/a3 -> :instruction "この振り分けが 1 回きりであることを 1 文で書く" :sample "This routing is a one-time decision per prompt; the agent does not switch modes mid-execution unless the user explicitly requests it.")
(defrule runtime-plan-subagent -> :nucleus runtime-plan-subagent/n :elaboration-additional runtime-plan-subagent/a1 :elaboration-additional runtime-plan-subagent/a2)
(defrule runtime-plan-subagent/n -> :instruction "計画を専用の部下のエージェントに任せる構えを 1 文で書く" :sample "Rather than switching the main agent into a restricted mode via dedicated plan-management tools, OpenDev delegates planning to a first-class Planner subagent.")
(defrule runtime-plan-subagent/a1 -> :instruction "計画が必要になったときに何を起動するかを 1 文で書く" :sample "When planning is needed, the main agent calls spawn_subagent(type=\"Planner\"), which launches a subagent with read-only tools and a specialized planning prompt.")
(defrule runtime-plan-subagent/a2 -> :instruction "書き込みの道具をどう扱うかと、その効果を 1 文で書く" :sample "Write operations are excluded from the subagent’s tool schema entirely: the LLM never sees tool definitions it cannot use, eliminating the possibility of write attempts during planning.")
(defrule runtime-planner-stages -> :nucleus runtime-planner-stages/n :elaboration-process-step runtime-planner-stages/a1 :elaboration-process-step runtime-planner-stages/a2 :elaboration-process-step runtime-planner-stages/a3)
(defrule runtime-planner-stages/n -> :instruction "計画役が行う段階の数を 1 文で書く" :sample "The Planner subagent executes in three stages visible in Figure 5.")
(defrule runtime-planner-stages/a1 -> :instruction "第 1 段階で何を調べるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "First, it explores the codebase using read-only tools: reading files, searching code, listing directory contents, and resolving symbol definitions.")
(defrule runtime-planner-stages/a2 -> :instruction "第 2 段階で何を分析するかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Second, it analyzes the findings, identifying patterns, evaluating risks, considering trade-offs, and determining the sequence of changes needed.")
(defrule runtime-planner-stages/a3 -> :instruction "第 3 段階で何を書き出すかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Third, it writes a structured plan to a file in the scratch directory, containing seven sections: goal, context, files to modify, new files to create, implementation steps, verification criteria, and risks.")
(defrule runtime-plan-review -> :nucleus runtime-plan-review/n :elaboration-additional runtime-plan-review/a1 :elaboration-additional runtime-plan-review/a2 :result runtime-plan-review/a3)
(defrule runtime-plan-review/n -> :instruction "計画役が終えたときに何を返すかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Upon completion, the Planner returns the plan file path to the main agent.")
(defrule runtime-plan-review/a1 -> :instruction "主のエージェントが計画をどう利用者に示すかを 1 文で書く" :sample "The main agent then calls present_plan(plan_file_path), which displays the plan to the user for review.")
(defrule runtime-plan-review/a2 -> :instruction "利用者の二つの選択を 1 文で書く" :sample "The user has two choices: revise (the main agent can spawn the Planner again with feedback) or approve (the agent proceeds to execution in Normal Mode).")
(defrule runtime-plan-review/a3 -> :instruction "この設計で要らなくなる状態を 1 文で書く" :sample "This design eliminates the need for a separate mode manager state: the main agent stays in Normal Mode throughout, and planning is simply a subagent delegation.")
(defrule runtime-normal -> :nucleus runtime-normal/n :elaboration-additional runtime-normal/a1 :elaboration-additional runtime-normal/a2)
(defrule runtime-normal/n -> :instruction "通常モードが既定で唯一の状態であることを 1 文で書く" :sample "Normal Mode is the default and only operating state.")
(defrule runtime-normal/a1 -> :instruction "通常モードで使える道具を 1 文で書く" :sample "The agent has full access to all tools, including file reading, file writing, code editing, command execution, and subagent spawning.")
(defrule runtime-normal/a2 -> :instruction "計画が承認された後の進め方を 1 文で書く" :sample "After a plan is approved via present_plan, the agent works through the planned steps, using the task management tools to track progress.")
(defrule runtime-replan -> :nucleus runtime-replan/n)
(defrule runtime-replan/n -> :instruction "実行中に予期しない結果に出会ったときの対処を 1 文で書く" :sample "During execution, if the agent encounters unexpected results (such as a test failure that reveals a deeper issue, a dependency conflict, or a scope change), it can spawn the Planner subagent again with the current codebase state as context, producing a revised plan that accounts for what has changed since the original plan was approved.")
(defrule runtime-old-design -> :nucleus runtime-old-design/n :elaboration-additional runtime-old-design/a1)
(defrule runtime-old-design/n -> :instruction "計画のために最初に採った設計と、その部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "The initial design used a four-tool state machine (enter_plan_mode, exit_plan_mode, create_plan, edit_plan) that switched the main agent into a restricted planning state.")
(defrule runtime-old-design/a1 -> :instruction "その設計が壊れやすかった具体的な様子を 1 文で書く" :sample "This was brittle: the agent sometimes failed to exit plan mode, leaving the system stuck in a read-only state requiring manual intervention.")
(defrule runtime-new-design -> :nucleus runtime-new-design/n :elaboration-additional runtime-new-design/a1 :elaboration-additional runtime-new-design/a2 :elaboration-additional runtime-new-design/a3)
(defrule runtime-new-design/n -> :instruction "今の設計がその状態機械を無くしたことを 1 文で書く" :sample "The current design eliminates this state machine entirely.")
(defrule runtime-new-design/a1 -> :instruction "計画を任せる先と、禁止の強制の位置を 1 文で書く" :sample "Planning is delegated to a Planner subagent with a schema that contains only read-only tools, enforcing the separation at the schema level rather than through runtime permission checks.")
(defrule runtime-new-design/a2 -> :instruction "書き込めない理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "The Planner cannot write because write tools do not exist in its schema, not because a runtime check blocks the attempt.")
(defrule runtime-new-design/a3 -> :instruction "得られる利点を 1 文で書く" :sample "This yields three advantages: (1) no state machine means no risk of getting stuck in plan mode; (2) the Planner can be spawned concurrently with other subagents (e.g., a Code Explorer for parallel analysis); and (3) the tool surface is reduced from four tools to one (present_plan), reducing cognitive load on the LLM.")
